# Next Directions

## Purpose

Keep plausible future work separate from current tasks and accepted decisions. A listed direction is not a commitment.

## Candidate register

| Candidate | Why it may matter | Evidence needed | Activation condition | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| No project-specific direction confirmed | Avoid inventing work during initialization. | User scope or project evidence | User declares the direction as active work | Unconfirmed |

## Adding a direction

- Describe the question or opportunity, not an assumed solution.
- State what evidence would justify the work.
- Identify dependencies, risks, and the condition that promotes it to `CURRENT_TASKS`.
- Move an activated direction to the task register and keep a traceable note here.

## Maintenance

Update when a plausible direction appears, changes, becomes active, or is retired.
